lesson: 171
title: The unknown on both sides of a story
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Sometimes the unknown number appears twice: 3 bags and 5 more weigh as much as 1 bag and 21 more.
explain: Take the same from both sides, like on a balance: take 1 bag away from each side, then 5 from each side.
explain: What is left says 2 bags = 21 - 5 = 16, so one bag is 16 / 2 = 8.
vars: a=name b=name x=3..30 m=2..5 p=1..20
let: q = (m - 1) * x + p
answer: x
exercise: I think of a number. If I multiply it by {m} and add {p}, I get the same as when I add {q} to it. What is my number?
exercise: {m} equal boxes of pencils and {p} loose pencils make as many pencils as 1 such box and {q} loose pencils. How many pencils are in one box?
exercise: {a} buys {m} notebooks and a pen for {p} dollars. {b} buys one notebook of the same kind and a game for {q} dollars. They pay the same. How many dollars does one notebook cost?
exercise: On a balance, {m} equal cubes and a {p} g weight on the left balance 1 cube and a {q} g weight on the right. How many grams does one cube weigh?
exercise: {a} has some stickers. If {a.he} had {m} times as many and then got {p} more, {a.he} would have {q} more than {a.he} has now. How many stickers does {a.he} have?
exercise: A number times {m}, plus {p}, equals the same number plus {q}. Find the number.
test: Adding {q} to a mystery number gives exactly what you get by adding {p} to {m} times the mystery number. What is the mystery number?
test: The left pan holds one jar of jam and {q} grams of weights; the right pan holds {m} jars just like it and {p} grams of weights. The scales are level. What does one jar weigh in grams?
test: {b} said: «My age multiplied by {m} and then increased by {p} is the same as my age increased by {q}.» How old is {b}?
test: A packet of seeds plus {q} loose seeds is as many seeds as {m} packets plus {p} loose seeds. Every packet holds the same number. How many seeds are in a packet?
exercise: Multiply a number by {m} and add {p}: you get the same result as adding {q} to the number. What is the number?
exercise: What number gives the same answer whether you multiply it by {m} and add {p}, or just add {q} to it?
exercise: {m} bags of marbles and {p} loose marbles hold as many marbles as one bag of the same size and {q} loose marbles. How many marbles are in one bag?
exercise: {a} buys {m} comics and a poster for {p} dollars at a shop in Ohio. {b} buys one comic at the same price and a game for {q} dollars. They spend the same amount. How much does one comic cost, in dollars?
exercise: On one pan of a balance in a classroom in Leeds there are {m} identical blocks and {p} grams; on the other there is 1 block with {q} grams. The pans are level. What does one block weigh, in grams?
exercise: Apples are packed in equal crates: {m.words} crates and {p} loose apples make as many apples as 1 crate and {q} loose apples. How many apples are in a crate?
exercise: {m} times a number, increased by {p}, is equal to the number increased by {q}. What is the number?
exercise: If {a} had {m} times as many buttons as {a.he} has and then {p} more, {a.he} would have exactly {q} buttons more than {a.he} has now. How many buttons does {a.he} have?
test: {b} from Sydney says: «If you add {q} to my number, you get the same as adding {p} to {m} times my number.» What is {b}'s number?
test: One box of chalk and {q} sticks of chalk make as many sticks as {m} boxes and {p} sticks. Each box holds the same number of sticks. How many sticks does a box hold?
test: At a café in Toronto, {m} muffins and a drink for {p} dollars cost the same as one muffin and a sandwich for {q} dollars. How many dollars is one muffin?
test: A scale is balanced: on the right, one toy car and {q} grams of weights; on the left, {m} toy cars like it and {p} grams of weights. How much does one toy car weigh, in grams?
test: Find the number that, added to {q}, gives the same result as {m} times the number added to {p}.
test: {a}'s age in years, taken {m} times and then plus {p}, equals {a.his} age plus {q}. How old is {a}?
exercise: think of a number, times {m}, add {p}, same as number plus {q}. what's the number
exercise: {m} boxes o pencils n {p} loose = 1 box n {q+1} — no wait, {q} loose. how many in a box
exercise: Sam says add em, {q}+{p}={q+p}. nah that's wrong innit. {m} boxes n {p} loose same as 1 box n {q} loose, how many in a box
exercise: {a} got {m} notebooks n a pen for {p} dollar, {b} got 1 notebook n a game for {q}, same money, oh and the shop shut at 6. how much 1 notebook
test: {m} bags plus {p} kg same as 1 bag plus {q} kg. bag weighs how much
test: {a} paid for {m} same packs plus {p} dollar, {b} paid 1 pack plus {q} dollar, same total. pack cost?
test: my number times {m+1}, no sorry, times {m}, plus {p}, equals the number plus {q}. what number
exercise: Grandad passed away and left his coins in equal boxes. {a} got {m} full boxes and {p} loose coins; {b} got 1 full box and {q} loose coins, and that was just as many. How many coins are in one box?
exercise: {a} was economical with the truth, said {a.he} had loads of stickers. turns out {a.he}'s got {m} packets and {p} loose, same as {b}'s 1 packet and {q} loose. how many in a packet, ya numpty
test: A charity shop sells "pre-loved" jars of buttons, all holding the same number. {m} jars plus {p} loose buttons equal 1 jar plus {q} loose buttons. How many buttons does a jar hold?
exam: It is given that a certain number, when multiplied by {m} and increased by {p}, yields the same result as when it is increased by {q}. Determine the number.
exam: Whereas {m} identical boxes of pencils together with {p} loose pencils contain as many pencils as one such box together with {q} loose pencils, ascertain the number of pencils in a single box.
exam: Ascertain the value of the unknown number, given that {m.words} times the number, increased by {p}, is equal to the number increased by {q}.
exam: {a} possesses {m} bags of marbles and {p} loose marbles, whereas {b} possesses one bag of the same size and {q} loose marbles. It being given that their holdings are equal, state the number of marbles in one bag.
